  "unresolved_mathematical_obligations": [
    "A true topological fiber bundle requires projection, local trivializations, transition cocycles and compatibility.",
    "No spectral tensor metric, energy, orientation or isometry theorem follows from reconstruction alone.",
    "Finite one-step Gibbs sampling law and finite deterministic uniform benchmark have candidate declarations. Independent draws, concentration, equidistribution, infinite-dimensional measure, and cusp-limit convergence remain unproved; AddDissociated.randomisation remains unused without support hypotheses.",
    "The one-sided all-positive-rate bound for the complete original signed Möbius pickup or endpointSum on adequately covering scales remains OPEN.",
    "General maximal coupling existence for a nonuniform Gibbs row is not established. The exact common-index overlap is a capacity, and only a uniform-row diagonal witness has been constructed.",
    "The sharp finite TV bound controls [0,1]-valued masked two-bit and unavailable-indicator observables, not the complete unbounded signed off-diagonal arithmetic source or any good-scale exponent.",
    "Exact maximal coupling for arbitrary nonuniform Gibbs rows and signed source importance sampling are SOURCE PROOF CANDIDATES and require a pinned Lean compile/kernel proof before accepted status.",
    "Full original-window importance correction requires the explicit full-support Gibbs row: every original endpoint index must have positive probability; sparse rows do not permit unconditional exact recovery.",
    "The signed source importance variance includes the entire inverse-weight second moment; finite TV control of bounded bit observables supplies no numerical bound on that variance or pickupCross.",
    "No arithmetic one-sided all-positive-rate upper bound or affine good-scale certificate for PickupEndpointQuadrature.endpointSum has been obtained."
